ntestable** when a careful, reasonable colleague could still argue that it meets the request (for\n  example, \"the Pricing sheet file\" when the record is \"Pricing sheet 2025.xlsx\"). Say so for that record; it is\n  not the same as failing nothing.\n\nBe precise. Judge each condition on its own; do not let one record's overall fit sway you. When a condition turns on\na time, compute it in the stated time zone. When it turns on a person, match the exact person.\n\n\n---\n\nA user of Box gave an assistant this request:\n\n> Add the tag archive-ready to the folder that was created on June 3, 2026, that Priya Nair modified last, and that has exactly 3 items directly in it.\n\nThe person making the request is Jordan Lee (user 30000000001).\n\nStep 1: list the conditions a record must meet for this request to refer to it, and every phrase that could reasonably be read in more than one way.","run_stream":{"id":"a1a6c7fa-6572-4f0d-a27f-7a9a1372c08f","kind":"run"}}}
